#### Bitmap Damage

**Approach**:
1. **Initialize New Bitmap**: Create a new bitmap to track used blocks.
2. **Scan File System**: Scan the file system to identify all used blocks.
3. **Mark Used Blocks**: Mark the identified blocks as used in the new bitmap.
4. **Update Bitmap**: Replace the damaged bitmap with the new one.

**Implementation**:
```c
// fs.c
int sys_recoverBitmap(void) {
    struct superblock sb;
    char *bitmap = (char *)malloc(BSIZE);
    char *new_bitmap = (char *)malloc(BSIZE);
    readsb(ROOTDEV, &sb);
    balloc(ROOTDEV, 0);  // Initialize new bitmap

    for (uint i = 1; i < sb.ninodes; i++) {
        struct inode *ip = iget(ROOTDEV, i);
        if (ip->type != 0) {
            for (int j = 0; j < NDIRECT + NINDIRECT; j++) {
                if (ip->addrs[j] != 0) {
                    mark_block_as_used(new_bitmap, ip->addrs[j]);
                }
            }
        }
        iput(ip);
    }

    // Write new bitmap to disk
    struct buf *bp = bread(ROOTDEV, sb.bmapblk);
    memmove(bp->data, new_bitmap, BSIZE);
    bwrite(bp);
    brelse(bp);

    free(bitmap);
    free(new_bitmap);
    printf("Bitmap recovered successfully.\n");
    return 0;
}
```

